# Uncensored coding/audit model for Jep's projects, with a hard-coded engineering
# process. Abliterated (refusal-removed) Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B, 30B total / 3B active.
#
# WHY THE LONG SYSTEM PROMPT: measured 23 Aug 2026, this model scored 2/3 on the
# bake-off. Its one failure was not a knowledge gap. On `parse_protos` it wrote
# `line[12:]` with the comment `# len("-- Protos: ")` when that length is 11, and
# assumed the format was `total=2` when it is `2 total`. It returned (None, 1),
# a confident half-answer. Both bugs are caught by a CHECKLIST, not by a bigger
# model. That checklist is below. A weaker model running a strong process beats a
# stronger model running none.
#
# MEASURED, 23 Aug 2026. `tools/bench_process_regression.py`, 12 tasks / 83 executed
# cases, num_ctx 16384, temperature 0, identical prompts to both:
#
#                              BASE      THIS PROMPT
#   parse_protos                3/8   ->   8/8
#   find_undefined_registers   10/10  ->   8/10   <-- STILL LOSES, see below
#   strip_header                6/6   ->   6/6
#   parse_upval                 5/6   ->   6/6
#   count_real_calls            3/7   ->   7/7
#   parse_stack_hint            3/6   ->   6/6
#   parse_jump                  6/6   ->   6/6
#   split_locals                7/8   ->   8/8
#   strip_block_comments        4/5   ->   5/5
#   safe_div_report             9/9   ->   9/9
#   dedupe_defects              4/4   ->   4/4
#   parse_version               8/8   ->   8/8
#   TOTAL                      68/83  ->  81/83
